From: Massimo Rigoselli <Massimo.Rigoselli () italtel ! it>
Date: Mon, 10 Jul 2000 12:51:31 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: HSZ70 and 36Gb disk drives
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96323345712259

Many thanks to Alan, Jef, Judith, Stephen, Ben, Scott, Rochelle,
Gregory, Martin and Hank who replyied to my question:

> does anyone know if HSZ70 RAID Array Controller supports 36 Gb
DS-RZ21FC-VW disk drives?

As Alan said, the right part number was DS-RZ1FC-VW, and the device type
supported depends on the firmware level (HSOF) too, not just the
hardware.

Martin said: "The 36GB disks DS-RZ1FB-VW/DS-RZ1FC-VW are supported (see
Compaq SPD 64.81.08) with HSZ70 and HSOF V7.7z.
There are also inoffical statements that they are working okay even with
V7.3z."

Hank said: "Check your firmware on the controllers. I'm old v7.3 and up
will support it, but 7.3 has some bugs. I upgraded mine to 7.7 before
plugging in the  36GB disks."

I was also interested about a 36Gb hot spare device in a cabinet with
18Gb based raidset.
About that Stephen said: "A 36Gb disk is fine as a hot spare for
anything which will fit but it is a waste of space as, in your case,
only 18Gb would be used and the remaining 18Gb would not be available
for any other purpose."

Massimo

