My original question was :-

>I want to add a user with a login of more than 8 characters
>Is this possible ?


>I  have tried adding a user, e.g. longname and theme editing the /etc/passwd
>file and changing it to longname1 (9 chars) - but I then cant login as
>either longname or longname1 (not suprising really)

>Is there a solution / workaround  to this problem ?


The recommend solution was to install C2 security and change to ENHANCED 
security.

Hovwever I also received the following email from Dr. Thomas P. Blinn
+ UNIX Software Group + Compaq Computer Corporation

All kinds of things in older releases KNOW that user names can not be
more than 8 characters.  There is no workaround.  Support for longer
user names is planned for a future release -- but I don't think it's
in V5.1, due out later this year.  However, in that release, all of
the standard utilities have been built to be able to support up to a
64 character login name (see the definitions in /usr/include/limits.h).

I have yet to try th C2 security option.

