Admins,
the problem seems to be solved now:

I configured lp1 (normal hp queue),
 configured lp2 (the filtering stuff) as:
 lp2|2|hp2:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp2err:\
        :lp=/dev/null:\
        :if=/var/spool/lpd2/pclfilter:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd2:

 for lp1 you should set rp to
        :rp=text:\
 to fix the stairstepping.

 in /var/spool/lpd2/pclfilter is:

 #!/bin/sh
 /bin/cat /var/spool/lpd2/pcl - | lp -d lp16

 in /var/spool/lpd2 is:
 ^[18H			------> THIS IS WERE IT WENT WRONG:
				------> It shouldn't be 18 (eighteen) but l
8: lowercase L - eight :-(
				------> Thx to Richard N. Frank's reply
 where the ^[ stands for the correct escape char,
 entered by hitting <ctrl>v and then the <esc> key

 Print the job to lp2: it works fine!

Regards,
Alex
BTW: a reset code does not seem to be nessecary...


