Mike D Cross [crossmd@mh.uk.sbphrd.com] wrote:
-----------------------------------------------
Hi,

Its a known problem with cron. It appears that cron forks to start
a cron job, it runs a routine to become the user of the job to run.
If for any reason the users files disappear during this phase, cron
does not give an error - it just leaves the forked process running as
root and you see the problem you are

If you cann Compaq they should be able to send you a patched version
of CRON, which avoids the problem - however it does not explain the 
root cause of the problem.

Mike

Alay Shah shahal@allegiance.net wrote:
-----------------------------------------
We had this problem on our site. Although I cannot recall exactly what the 
problem was i.e Multiple cron processes or crontab firing up the same job 
several times. However, we have a patch that fixed the problem on our site.
See 
if you can call support and ask for this patch. This patch had the same fix
for 
V4.0D, E and F.

BCGMC1ZNX.tar

Good Luck!

